  "full_text": "So if you say short sentences, it's easy to be profound. As a matter of fact, the less you say, the more profound you can be. Maybe you can imagine it as a vibrating guitar string, and the more places you hold it, it's not a good analogy but because why is it not a good analogy because uh only takes about doesn't take very many fixed points to stop a guitar string i was kind of looking for a useful way to explain clamping down clamping down you know i think the guitar string is pretty good so i don't know Oh, well. So, no, there's got to be a... So, normal people are normal smart people. I'm not a smart person. I normally just... But you know what? Fuck you. I'm convinced that everything that I lack, I make up for in something different, you know? Like being... You know how nerds are kind of like, lack one thing, get something else. Anyway, so what's a good metaphor for if you have one word, if you have two words, if you have three words, if you have four words, how much? Basically, if you plan it out, you're a fucking Christian, for God's sake. The sweet taste of success. He who trusts in his riches will fall, but the righteous will flourish like a green leaf. Our society has gorged itself on the sweet taste of success. We've filled our plates from the buffet of books that range from dressing for success to investing for success. We've gobbled down stacks of notebooks, cassette albums, and videotapes in our hunger for greater success. The irony is that all is that Instead of fulfillment, we experience a bloated sensation of being full of ourselves, our dreams, our goals, our plans, our projects, our accomplishments. The result of this all-you-can-eat appetite is not contentment, it's nausea.",
